---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="peon.dev — post-mortem"
	description="Peon was a virtual colleague for developers. It worked great before the AI era. We are shutting it down for good. Thank you."
>
	<main class="pm">
		<header class="head">
			<div class="logo"><pre class="ascii" aria-hidden="true">
 ██████╗ ███████╗ ██████╗ ███╗   ██╗
 ██╔══██╗██╔════╝██╔═══██╗████╗  ██║
 ██████╔╝█████╗  ██║   ██║██╔██╗ ██║
 ██╔═══╝ ██╔══╝  ██║   ██║██║╚██╗██║
 ██║     ███████╗╚██████╔╝██║ ╚████║
 ╚═╝     ╚══════╝ ╚═════╝ ╚═╝  ╚═══╝</pre><span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">decommissioned</span></div>
			<h1 class="sr">Peon post-mortem</h1>

			<dl class="meta">
				<dt>document</dt><dd>POST-MORTEM #001 — the last one</dd>
				<dt>service</dt><dd>peon.dev</dd>
				<dt>severity</dt><dd><span class="tag dead">SEV-0 / permanent</span></dd>
				<dt>status</dt><dd><span class="tag ok">RESOLVED</span> <span class="dim">— by shutting down</span></dd>
				<dt>uptime</dt><dd>2021-07 → 2026-10</dd>
			</dl>
		</header>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="n">01</span> tl;dr</h2>
			<p class="lead">
				Peon was a great tool built on a great idea. It worked really well — <em>before AI</em>.
				Today it no longer pulls its weight, and I don't have the energy left to rebuild it for the AI
				era. So I'm shutting peon.dev down. For good.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="n">02</span> what peon was</h2>
			<p>
				A virtual colleague for developers. You told it what to do. It did the task on a schedule, opened a
				merge request, and you reviewed it, merged it, and went back to the work that mattered.
			</p>
			<ul class="list">
				<li>fix coding standards, remove dead code, update dependencies</li>
				<li>run Rector, add type hints, fix deprecations</li>
				<li>anything that runs in a shell — if it changed code, you got a merge request</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				It started out as <span class="hl">PHPMate</span>, grew into <span class="hl">Peon</span>, and was
				<a href="https://github.com/peon-dev">100% open source</a> all along.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="n">03</span> timeline</h2>
			<ol class="log">
				<li><time>2021-07</time><span class="lvl info">INFO</span><span>PHPMate is born. Mission: give developers their time back.</span></li>
				<li><time>2021-07</time><span class="lvl ok">OK</span><span>Carvago hands Rector over to the bot. <b>~30 min saved per developer, every day.</b></span></li>
				<li><time>later</time><span class="lvl ok">OK</span><span>Renamed to Peon. Recipes, custom tasks, open source.</span></li>
				<li><time>2023</time><span class="lvl warn">WARN</span><span>AI coding assistants arrive. The bar for "automation" moves overnight.</span></li>
				<li><time>2025</time><span class="lvl warn">WARN</span><span>Agents now open their own merge requests. Peon's unique edge gets thin.</span></li>
				<li><time>2026-10</time><span class="lvl dead">FATAL</span><span>Maintainer energy budget exhausted. Graceful shutdown started.</span></li>
			</ol>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="n">04</span> what went well</h2>
			<ul class="list plus">
				<li>The idea was right: boring, repeatable work belongs to a machine, not a person.</li>
				<li>The workflow matched how teams already work: task → merge request → review → merge.</li>
				<li>It saved real hours for real teams, and made developers a bit happier.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="n">05</span> root cause</h2>
			<p>
				No single bug. The world just changed. Peon was built for a time when automation meant
				<em>deterministic scripts on a schedule</em>. Now an AI agent can read a codebase, reason about
				it, and fix things no script ever could. Next to that, Peon lacks the utility to be worth running.
			</p>
			<p>
				Bringing it into the AI era would not be a patch. It would be a rewrite. With other, bigger
				projects to run, I can't give it the energy it would need. Better to end it honestly than to let it
				rot quietly.
			</p>
			<p class="callout">
				<span class="dim">contributing factors:</span> AI ate the use case · finite energy · bigger projects
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="n">06</span> action items</h2>
			<ul class="list check">
				<li><s>rewrite peon for the AI era</s> <span class="dim">— won't fix</span></li>
				<li>shut down peon.dev <span class="tag ok">done</span></li>
				<li>keep the source code public on <a href="https://github.com/peon-dev">github.com/peon-dev</a> <span class="tag ok">done</span></li>
				<li>say thank you <span class="tag ok">done ↓</span></li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="thanks">
			<h2><span class="n">07</span> thank you</h2>
			<p class="big">
				To everyone who used Peon, filed an issue, sent feedback, merged one of its merge requests, or
				just believed in the idea — <span class="hl">thank you.</span>
			</p>
			<p>It was a good run, and I'm proud of what it did. ♥</p>
			<p class="contact">
				<span class="dim">// if you want to get in touch, reach me at</span><br />
				<a href="mailto:j.mikes@me.com">j.mikes@me.com</a>
			</p>
			<p class="sig">— Jan Mikeš</p>
		</section>

		<footer class="foot">
			<pre><span class="dim">$</span> systemctl stop peon.dev
<span class="dim">$</span> systemctl disable peon.dev
<span class="ok">✓</span> peon.dev stopped. exit code 0.
<span class="dim">$</span> <span class="cursor">█</span></pre>
		</footer>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.pm {
		max-width: 46rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 4rem 1.25rem 5rem;
	}

	.sr {
		position: absolute;
		width: 1px;
		height: 1px;
		overflow: hidden;
		clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
	}

	.logo {
		position: relative;
		display: inline-block;
		margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
	}

	.ascii {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: clamp(0.5rem, 2.2vw, 0.85rem);
		line-height: 1.1;
		color: var(--dim);
		opacity: 0.6;
	}

	.stamp {
		position: absolute;
		right: -0.75rem;
		bottom: -0.6rem;
		padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
		border: 2px solid var(--dead);
		color: var(--dead);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		letter-spacing: 0.15em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		transform: rotate(-6deg);
		background: var(--bg);
	}

	.meta {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
		gap: 0.15rem 1.5rem;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 1rem 0;
		border-top: 1px dashed var(--faint);
		border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--faint);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}

	.meta dt {
		color: var(--dim);
	}

	.meta dt::after {
		content: ':';
	}

	.meta dd {
		margin: 0;
	}

	section {
		margin-top: 3.5rem;
	}

	h2 {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--fg);
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	h2::after {
		content: '';
		flex: 1;
		height: 1px;
		background: var(--faint);
	}

	.n {
		color: var(--accent);
	}

	.n::before {
		content: '§';
		margin-right: 0.25rem;
		color: var(--dim);
	}

	p {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}

	.lead {
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: #f1ede2;
	}

	em {
		font-style: italic;
		color: var(--warn);
	}

	.hl {
		color: var(--accent);
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.dim {
		color: var(--dim);
	}

	.ok {
		color: var(--ok);
	}

	.tag {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0 0.4rem;
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		border: 1px solid currentColor;
	}

	.tag.dead {
		color: var(--dead);
	}

	.tag.ok {
		color: var(--ok);
	}

	.list {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		padding: 0;
	}

	.list li {
		position: relative;
		padding-left: 1.75rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
	}

	.list li::before {
		content: '-';
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		color: var(--dim);
	}

	.list.plus li::before {
		content: '+';
		color: var(--ok);
	}

	.list.check li::before {
		content: '[x]';
		color: var(--ok);
		left: -0.6rem;
	}

	.list.check li:first-child::before {
		content: '[-]';
		color: var(--dim);
	}

	s {
		color: var(--dim);
	}

	.log {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		font-size: 0.88rem;
		border-left: 1px solid var(--faint);
	}

	.log li {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 4.75rem 3.5rem 1fr;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		padding: 0.45rem 0 0.45rem 1rem;
	}

	.log time {
		color: var(--dim);
	}

	.log b {
		color: var(--ok);
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.lvl {
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		padding-top: 0.1rem;
	}

	.lvl.info {
		color: var(--accent);
	}

	.lvl.ok {
		color: var(--ok);
	}

	.lvl.warn {
		color: var(--warn);
	}

	.lvl.dead {
		color: var(--dead);
	}

	.log li:last-child {
		background: rgba(229, 83, 75, 0.08);
	}

	.callout {
		padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
		border-left: 2px solid var(--warn);
		background: rgba(242, 184, 75, 0.05);
		font-size: 0.88rem;
	}

	.thanks {
		margin-top: 4.5rem;
		padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--faint);
		background: #11110f;
	}

	.big {
		font-size: 1.2rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: #f1ede2;
	}

	.contact {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}

	.sig {
		margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
		color: var(--accent);
	}

	.foot {
		margin-top: 4rem;
	}

	.foot pre {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		line-height: 1.8;
		white-space: pre-wrap;
	}

	.cursor {
		animation: blink 1.1s steps(1) infinite;
		color: var(--fg);
	}

	@keyframes blink {
		50% {
			opacity: 0;
		}
	}

	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
		.cursor {
			animation: none;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 34rem) {
		.pm {
			padding-top: 2.5rem;
		}

		.log li {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 0;
		}

		.lvl {
			display: none;
		}

		.thanks {
			padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
		}
	}
</style>
